---Project-level rolling release configuration that defines how deployments should be gradually rolled out
---@class vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingRelease
---@field canaryResponseHeader? boolean Whether the request served by a canary deployment should return a header indicating a canary was served. Defaults to `false` when omitted.
---@field gate? vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseGate Automated gating configuration. Omitted (the default) means no gating is configured, which is equivalent to `enabled: false`.
---@field stages? vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseStagesList|distilled.Null An array of all the stages required during a deployment release. Each stage defines a target percentage and advancement rules. The final stage must always have targetPercentage: 100.
---@field target string The environment that the release targets, currently only supports production. Adding in case we want to configure with alias groups or custom environments.

---Automated gating configuration. Omitted (the default) means no gating is configured, which is equivalent to `enabled: false`.
---@class vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseGate
---@field action vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseGateAction What to do when the gate trips: pause the rollout, or roll it back.
---@field checks vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseGateChecksList The checks to evaluate. An empty array means nothing is evaluated.
---@field dryRun boolean When true, a tripped gate is only reported — {@link action} is not taken.
---@field enabled boolean Whether automated gating is enabled for this project's rollouts.
---@field failureThreshold? number How many failing evaluations within {@link windowSize} trip the gate. Defaults to `3` when omitted.
---@field windowSize? number How many of the most recent evaluations {@link failureThreshold} is counted against. Defaults to `5` when omitted.

---What to do when the gate trips: pause the rollout, or roll it back.
---@alias vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseGateAction "pause"|"rollback"

---The checks to evaluate. An empty array means nothing is evaluated.
---@class vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseGateChecksItem
---@field excludePaths? vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseGateChecksItemExcludePathsList Request paths to ignore entirely — dropped from both the numerator (errors) and the denominator (total requests). Matched exactly against the request path with any query string removed; no prefix or glob matching. Defaults to `[]` when omitted.
---@field excludeStatusCodes? vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseGateChecksItemExcludeStatusCodesList Response status codes to ignore entirely — dropped from both the numerator (errors) and the denominator (total requests). Defaults to `[]` when omitted.
---@field ingestWatermarkSeconds? number Seconds of ingest lag to allow for: the query's upper bound is `now() - this value`, so the check never reads a window that is still filling. Defaults to `30` when omitted.
---@field significanceLevel? number A run fails only when the canary's error rate is higher and its one-sided Fisher p-value is below this significance level. Defaults to `0.05`; lower values require stronger evidence.
---@field type vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseGateChecksItemType The metric this check evaluates.

---Request paths to ignore entirely — dropped from both the numerator (errors) and the denominator (total requests). Matched exactly against the request path with any query string removed; no prefix or glob matching. Defaults to `[]` when omitted.
---@alias vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseGateChecksItemExcludePathsList string[]

---Response status codes to ignore entirely — dropped from both the numerator (errors) and the denominator (total requests). Defaults to `[]` when omitted.
---@alias vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseGateChecksItemExcludeStatusCodesList number[]

---The metric this check evaluates.
---@alias vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseGateChecksItemType "error-rate-5xx"

---The checks to evaluate. An empty array means nothing is evaluated.
---@alias vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseGateChecksList vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseGateChecksItem[]

---An array of all the stages required during a deployment release. Each stage defines a target percentage and advancement rules. The final stage must always have targetPercentage: 100.
---@class vercel.projects.CreateProjectResponseRollingReleaseStagesItem
---@field duration? number Duration in minutes for automatic advancement to the next stage
---@field linearShift? boolean Whether to linearly shift traffic over the duration of this stage
---@field requireApproval? boolean Whether or not this stage requires manual approval to proceed
---@field targetPercentage number The percentage of traffic to serve to the canary deployment (0-100)

